How do these three techniques compare in terms of speed over line?

58:49.820 --> 58:56.780
I mean, if you think about the computation behind all these techniques is extremely fast.

58:56.780 --> 59:02.220
So in terms of speed, they are all, nowadays with current processors, extremely fast.

59:03.500 --> 59:11.500
RANSAC has this advantage of being capable of being robust to outliers. So when you are in

59:11.500 --> 59:16.700
situations with a lot of outliers, RANSAC tends to be more robust, so preferable to QTransform.

59:17.260 --> 59:22.460
But RANSAC has all these additional parameters to tune, like W, the threshold, and so on.

59:23.340 --> 59:29.740
While this method is a bit less robust, does not have a statistical interpretation,

